  "edges": [],
  "description": "R35 (the DEPTH MATRIX in the place vector: the ToF's own 8x8 (64 zone ranges) instead of 8 column ranges (the control arm for the camera)), from a1v2_r34_h2_head_joints.json: 2026-09-11, the exploration line's control arm: today's place vector is [x, y, cos, sin, 8 column ranges], so what tells one map node from another is mostly the odometry (a grid over a path integral wearing an EPM). Before the camera (C2) the cheapest richer geometry is the sensor's own 8x8 depth matrix, on the wire on the real robot: the same place vector with the 64 zone slant ranges / 4 m (Empty = 4 m) in place of the 8 columns. The host reads the width from map_epm.proprio_state_dims (12 or 68); nothing else changes. Judged on the star HEAD stack in the playroom, n = 6, paired with R34: nodes vs cells (does the map separate places, or just odometry cells), map TLE, walls/min, objs/min, down%. A camera arm (C2) then has this to beat."
